From: Luna Nova <git@lunnova.dev>
Date: Sat, 7 Feb 2026 00:48:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] rocm-runtime: fix crash in QueueCreate due to trying to free non allocated scratch

if (scratch.main_queue_base != nullptr) before calling ReleaseQueueMainScratch
because ReleaseQueueMainScratch is only valid if main_queue_base is set
and the scope guard can fire for an error allocating the queue.

(cherry picked from ROCm/rocm-systems commit b7717446c85d, pull request #2850,
merged 2026-02-07; the message above is the author's)
[Artur Andrzejczak: ported to the rocr-runtime 7.1.1 source layout that
 Fedora's package builds from, only the path prefix changed; with Claude
 Fable 5.1 (Anthropic)]
Link: https://github.com/ROCm/rocm-systems/pull/2850
Signed-off-by: Artur Andrzejczak <andrzejczak.artur@gmail.com>
---
--- a/projects/rocr-runtime/runtime/hsa-runtime/core/runtime/amd_gpu_agent.cpp
+++ b/projects/rocr-runtime/runtime/hsa-runtime/core/runtime/amd_gpu_agent.cpp
@@ -1772,11 +1772,16 @@
   scratch.main_queue_base = nullptr;
   scratch.main_queue_process_offset = 0;
 
-  MAKE_NAMED_SCOPE_GUARD(scratchGuard, [&]() { ReleaseQueueMainScratch(scratch); });
+  MAKE_NAMED_SCOPE_GUARD(scratchGuard, [&]() {
+    if (scratch.main_queue_base != nullptr) ReleaseQueueMainScratch(scratch);
+  });
 
   if (scratch.main_size != 0) {
     AcquireQueueMainScratch(scratch);
     if (scratch.main_queue_base == nullptr) {
+      LogPrint(HSA_AMD_LOG_FLAG_INFO,
+               "Failed to allocate scratch memory for queue, size=%zu, node=%u",
+               scratch.main_size, node_id());
       return HSA_STATUS_ERROR_OUT_OF_RESOURCES;
     }
   }
